{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs","id":1384879,"title":"[V5] Houserule: No More Opportunity Costs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T11:39:36-07:00","id":1384879,"title":"[V5] Houserule: No More Opportunity Costs","content":"As currently written, V5's discipline powers are balanced around opportunity costs. Every power you buy makes other powers more expensive, and you can never have more than five powers in a single Discipline, ever. The thematic justification is because every power involves &quot;calcifying&quot; your blood into new patterns in an irreversible way. But it also means that an elder Gangrel would find it harder to learn a new first-level Protean power than a neonate Ventrue, which is a bit different from earlier editions (where elders tended to have lots of combination disciplines for unique effects).<br /> <br /> So as an alternative\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Rule: No More Opportunity Costs</b><br /> <br /> Under this optional rule, characters are no longer limited to five powers in any given Discipline. Instead of purchasing Discipline dots directly, they purchase individual powers: an in-clan power costs 5\u00d7level, an out-of-clan power costs 7\u00d7level, and a Caitiff power costs 6\u00d7level. All normal rules about learning Disciplines (using resonances and/or a teacher's blood) still apply.<br /> <br /> A character's <b>rating</b> in a Discipline is the level of the highest power they have in that Discipline, and this is the value used when constructing dice pools. Their <b>proficiency</b> in a Discipline is the total number of powers they have in that Discipline; characters cannot purchase powers with a rating higher than their proficiency plus one.<br /> <br /> Example: Demetrios, a Malkavian, has no Auspex powers, so his Auspex rating and proficiency are both zero. He pays 5xp for <i>Heightened Senses</i>, a level-one power, and his Auspex rating and proficiency are now one. He pays another 5xp for <i>Sense the Unseen</i>, a level-one power; his proficiency is now two, but his rating remains one.<br /> <br /> When rolling for <i>Sense the Unseen</i>, he uses a single die to represent his Auspex in the die pool, since his rating is one. However, since his proficiency is now two, he can buy third-level powers like <i>Scry the Soul</i> if he wants (for 15xp each), since three is one higher than his proficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:55:34-07:00","id":1384900,"title":"","content":"The way I do it is similar. Once you buy a Discipline to a certain level, you can buy any Discipline power of that level or lower for the price of buying it all that level. So if you have, say, Protean three and picked Eyes of the Beast, Claws, and Earthmeld, you can now buy Shapechange for 15 xp, Weight of a Feather for 5 xp, and so forth. But you couldn't, say, skip over buying a 4rth level power and just go straight for a fifth. Not in my games, anyway, as I don't have a &quot;proficiency&quot; trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:25:05-07:00","id":1384908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384900#post1384900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I do it is similar. Once you buy a Discipline to a certain level, you can buy any Discipline power of that level or lower for the price of buying it all that level. So if you have, say, Protean three and picked Eyes of the Beast, Claws, and Earthmeld, you can now buy Shapechange for 15 xp, Weight of a Feather for 5 xp, and so forth. But you couldn't, say, skip over buying a 4rth level power and just go straight for a fifth. Not in my games, anyway, as I don't have a &quot;proficiency&quot; trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only issue with doing it that way is the &quot;gaps&quot; in the system. This would mean that, for example, anyone with Auspex &gt;1 will need to have Premonition, since there's no other power at that level. And I could imagine, say, a Toreador not wanting to spend 10xp on a Malkavian-themed power that doesn't fit their concept.<br /> <br /> Sometimes this can even have further-reaching repercussions. For example, Protean and Obfuscate both have prerequisites on their only fourth-level powers. So you'll have to go back and take those prereqs if you want to get to level five, making for a pretty heavy xp tax on e.g. a Tzimisce who's not interested in turning into animals.<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily a game-breaking problem (and this reply is meant more as a &quot;here's my rationale for doing it differently&quot; than as &quot;I don't like your idea&quot;)\u2014there were definitely &quot;speed bump&quot; powers in earlier editions, after all. But V5's tried hard to avoid that by putting multiple generally-useful powers at dot one for every discipline, so you can take those in any &quot;dead&quot; levels. That's the main reason I introduced proficiency alongside rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:35:49-07:00","id":1384912,"title":"","content":"Are you also increasing XP gained per game? Because disciplines are expensive, and what you've suggested makes you need to spend more if you wanted something additional in the low levels and a high level. For example I can't buy two 1's and a 3, I'd have to buy a 2 along the way, whilst that wouldn't be an issue in V5's basic system. <br /> <br /> In my opinion, you've gotta go completely one way or another. Either VTM linear disciplines, or you let players be DnD clerics with disciplines and choose what you've got upon rising each night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:08:44-07:00","id":1384917,"title":"","content":"The preregs are gone in my games as well. If you want to go straight from Earth Meld to Batform, you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:53:42-07:00","id":1384928,"title":"","content":"This is nice, I like how it fits the existing mechanics nicely but at the same time makes it simple to use. well done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384912#post1384912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you also increasing XP gained per game? Because disciplines are expensive, and what you've suggested makes you need to spend more if you wanted something additional in the low levels and a high level. For example I can't buy two 1's and a 3, I'd have to buy a 2 along the way, whilst that wouldn't be an issue in V5's basic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its actually cheaper in this house-rule not more expensive to buy disciplines.<br /> <br /> Old way: I buy level 1 Auspex for 5 points then level 2 Auspex, but choose the other level 1 power 10 points for a total of 15 then I buy the 3rd level and actually take the third for 15 points.<br /> <br /> I get 2 first level powers and 1 third for a total of 30 XP.<br /> <br /> House-rule way: I buy a level one power for 5 points then i buy the second level one for 5 instead of 10 points as it is a level one so I have spent 10 points instead of 15. now because I have two powers i can buy the level 3 power for 15 if I wish or the level two for 10. If I buy the level 3 then I spend 15 points.<br /> <br /> I get 2 first level powers and 1 third for a total of 25 XP rather than 30.<br /> <br /> Cheaper by he houseruled method. I really like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384912#post1384912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, you've gotta go completely one way or another. Either VTM linear disciplines, or you let players be DnD clerics with disciplines and choose what you've got upon rising each night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is wrong on many levels. but I will only go with one Drac just showed that there is more than these two methods for discipline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-30-2020, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:27:36-07:00","id":1384940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384912#post1384912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you also increasing XP gained per game? Because disciplines are expensive, and what you've suggested makes you need to spend more if you wanted something additional in the low levels and a high level. For example I can't buy two 1's and a 3, I'd have to buy a 2 along the way, whilst that wouldn't be an issue in V5's basic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been having some difficulty making the phrasing clear (you're not the only one to read it this way, so I need to do more editing), but my intent is that it's actually cheaper, as Redwulfe said. You can still buy two 1s and a 3, but it now costs 5+5+15 instead of 5+10+15.<br /> <br /> Now, separate from this, I do also increase XP gained per game, because one xp per session feels way too slow when you've got scaling xp costs. But that's a separate issue (and I'm still not very happy with the houserules I've got for it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:29:19-07:00","id":1384941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384917#post1384917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The preregs are gone in my games as well. If you want to go straight from Earth Meld to Batform, you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, interesting. Well, that's certainly one way to handle it! It still seems a bit weird that Tzimisce need to turn into a bat to get a level-five power, but adding some more options at every level would help with that. (Maybe Protean 4 gains a war-form option or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:50:08-07:00","id":1384946,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce turning into bats is nothing new, really...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:05:45-07:00","id":1384947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384941#post1384941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, interesting. Well, that's certainly one way to handle it! It still seems a bit weird that Tzimisce need to turn into a bat to get a level-five power, but adding some more options at every level would help with that. (Maybe Protean 4 gains a war-form option or something.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's supposed to be more powers in the PG, and I would expect Tzimisce to get a Vicissitude-based Level 4 amalgam in Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:36:54-07:00","id":1384955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs#post1384879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As currently written, V5's discipline powers are balanced around opportunity costs. Every power you buy makes other powers more expensive, and you can never have more than five powers in a single Discipline, ever. The thematic justification is because every power involves &quot;calcifying&quot; your blood into new patterns in an irreversible way. But it also means that an elder Gangrel would find it harder to learn a new first-level Protean power than a neonate Ventrue, which is a bit different from earlier editions (where elders tended to have lots of combination disciplines for unique effects).<br /> <br /> So as an alternative\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Rule: No More Opportunity Costs</b><br /> <br /> Under this optional rule, characters are no longer limited to five powers in any given Discipline. Instead of purchasing Discipline dots directly, they purchase individual powers: an in-clan power costs 5\u00d7level, an out-of-clan power costs 7\u00d7level, and a Caitiff power costs 6\u00d7level. All normal rules about learning Disciplines (using resonances and/or a teacher's blood) still apply.<br /> <br /> A character's <b>rating</b> in a Discipline is the level of the highest power they have in that Discipline, and this is the value used when constructing dice pools. Their <b>proficiency</b> in a Discipline is the total number of powers they have in that Discipline; characters cannot purchase powers with a rating higher than their proficiency plus one.<br /> <br /> Example: Demetrios, a Malkavian, has no Auspex powers, so his Auspex rating and proficiency are both zero. He pays 5xp for <i>Heightened Senses</i>, a level-one power, and his Auspex rating and proficiency are now one. He pays another 5xp for <i>Sense the Unseen</i>, a level-one power; his proficiency is now two, but his rating remains one.<br /> <br /> When rolling for <i>Sense the Unseen</i>, he uses a single die to represent his Auspex in the die pool, since his rating is one. However, since his proficiency is now two, he can buy third-level powers like <i>Scry the Soul</i> if he wants (for 15xp each), since three is one higher than his proficiency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, might need to propose this at my table! Will definitely reduce how much my characters agonize over picking powers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:09:33-07:00","id":1384969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384946#post1384946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce turning into bats is nothing new, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Tzimisce with Vicissitude 1 have always been able to turn into a bat. Gangrel just did it much, much, much faster.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:16:47-07:00","id":1384970,"title":"","content":"Why would they even make it so buying one discipline makes others more expensive? What is this &quot;calcifying&quot; blood thing? What is this, Onesong'd Vampires now? WTF","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:20:26-07:00","id":1384971,"title":"","content":"My storyteller is doing something similar. Yes, it can be time saving on exp, Oblivion is a good example, as you can get 4 level one powers and then a level 5 power. Drops the cost down to a total of 65 for in clan, (5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 25). <br /> <br /> I am not entirely sold on the idea, yet. I am plotting a combination of this and my own Elder idea.<br /> <br /> You purchase a dot of a discipline, when you do that, your dot rating increases and you can purchase powers in combination up to the level of the discipline dot you have purchased.<br /> First Dot = one level 1 power<br /> Second Dot = one level 2 power or two level 1 powers<br /> Third Dot = one level 3 power, one level 2 and one level 1, or three level 1<br /> And so on.<br /> Vampires of generation 7 (maybe 8, based on the chart) or lower can purchase up to their Blood Potency maximum in dots in an individual discipline.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect system, but does allow for having more than 5 powers per discipline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:41:21-07:00","id":1384975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SarcasticJazzHands</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384971#post1384971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You purchase a dot of a discipline, when you do that, your dot rating increases and you can purchase powers in combination up to the level of the discipline dot you have purchased.<br /> First Dot = one level 1 power<br /> Second Dot = one level 2 power or two level 1 powers<br /> Third Dot = one level 3 power, one level 2 and one level 1, or three level 1<br /> And so on.<br /> Vampires of generation 7 (maybe 8, based on the chart) or lower can purchase up to their Blood Potency maximum in dots in an individual discipline.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect system, but does allow for having more than 5 powers per discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only issue with this is it seems like you can run out of powers that add up right. For example, suppose I have four dots in something, and want another level-four power, but I already have all the level-ones.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you let people change up the combinations a bit when they buy a new level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:43:14-07:00","id":1384976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384970#post1384970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they even make it so buying one discipline makes others more expensive? What is this &quot;calcifying&quot; blood thing? What is this, Onesong'd Vampires now? WTF</div> </div> </div> </div>The metaphor is something like branches growing on a tree. The more a particular branch has already grown, the harder it is to force it into a new shape.<br /> <br /> I don't really like it, thematically, but it's part of the new Resonance system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:48:30-07:00","id":1384977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384969#post1384969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Tzimisce with Vicissitude 1 have always been able to turn into a bat. Gangrel just did it much, much, much faster.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vicissitude cannot alther you size more than 30cm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:00:23-07:00","id":1384980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384976#post1384976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The metaphor is something like branches growing on a tree. The more a particular branch has already grown, the harder it is to force it into a new shape.<br /> <br /> I don't really like it, thematically, but it's part of the new Resonance system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its horrible. Deliberate capping where it doesn't need to be at all. It really, really, doesn't make any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:00:53-07:00","id":1384981,"title":"","content":"I was referring to Chiropteran Marauder, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T20:25:22-07:00","id":1384993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384975#post1384975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only issue with this is it seems like you can run out of powers that add up right. For example, suppose I have four dots in something, and want another level-four power, but I already have all the level-ones.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you let people change up the combinations a bit when they buy a new level?</div> </div> </div> </div>With as mutable as the blood is now, it seems easy to come up with more powers. I believe we have at least 3 if not 4 level one powers of Oblivion now. Protean is looking like it will gain some Vissiccitude branching, no pun intended. You could also add powers like the Mariners had in previous versions. I actually see the blood not really calcifying as being even more mutable, as you are no longer locked into a specific powers like you were in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could apply unused power levels as bonus dice on lower level powers.<br /> <br /> Like I said, not completely finished with it but it is a work in progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:49:38-07:00","id":1385133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384879-v5-houserule-no-more-opportunity-costs?p=1384928#post1384928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is wrong on many levels. but I will only go with one Drac just showed that there is more than these two methods for discipline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 changed what was originally the fundamental linear disciplines set down by God/Caine/Lilith/TheAliens into a pick and choose. At this point you really might as well be DnD clerics and choose what powers you want for the night. It'd actually take a lot of the stress away from choosing what powers you want to be stuck with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T16:25:06-07:00","id":1385151,"title":"","content":"So now it seems your misunderstanding multiple game systems.<br /> <br /> First clerics don't work like that but I am not going into D&amp;D magic systems as it is not really worth it and...<br /> <br /> Second V5 did not do some sort of giant leap when it came to their Discipline power system. The concept of multiple powers at a given discipline level that is chosen by the player upon gaining that level started in Vampire in 1st edition with 6th level powers and above.<br /> <br /> page 76, Players guide 1991.<br /> &quot;Thus characters capable of achieving each ranking from six to ten have a variety of abilities available to them at each level. When they have had the experience necessary to obtain these powers, they may choose whichever power of that level they feel best fits their character.<br /> Also, as characters continue to progress in their disciplines, they may choose from any power of the rank they are achieving or lower.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not even remotely some sort of stretch to see that when they decided to bring 6+ level powers into the lower ranks they just brought the already existing since 1991 rule into the new system. The only thing new is that they squashed the powers into a 1-5 ranking adding even more player agency into the game. Not only was this not the first time that Vampire had a pick in choose system since backgrounds secondary skills, merits and flaws, gifts ad so on have been in the game for ever, also use the pick and choose mechanics, not to mention that Tremere had the pick n choose method added to Thaumaturgy with the advent of being able to start the game with a different path than what they started with but Caitiff got that by being able to pick in choose their discipline spreads. Sabbat have always had a virtual feast in the number of powers they could get by swapping with each other so it is not hard to see where this pick n choose style of play came from in Vampire it was 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 05-01-2020, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T00:58:49-07:00","id":1385211,"title":"","content":"All ratings of 1-5 are &quot;natural&quot;. Vampire powers that fall into this range are within God/Caine/Lilith/TheAliens view on things. Similarly, the other splats have 'normal' powers at 1-5, and anything at 6 and beyond has always been bizzare fuckery that's left mages stuck in the void and perhaps vampires stuck in torpor. For each generation beyond the third, vampires have had their power cap reduced by one (IE 5th gens have eight dots, sixth gens have seven dots, 7th gens have six dots...) But for the full range of 8th to 13th you've got vampires stuck with a maximum of 5... Why do you think that is? Why don't 9th gens have a discipline maximum of 4? Why aren't 10th gens capped at 3? Why is it that for a full five generations people are stuck at five levels of disciplines? <br /> Because the first five levels are natural and set down by a higher power. It's only when you go beyond the natural limitations can you transcend the standardized patern and pick your own powers. Did you think this was all a happy accident of game design or something? No, it's metaphysics. And V5 has looked at those 6+ powers and then thought &quot;Why can't 1-5 be like that?&quot; without the actual answer. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, V5 might as well have vampires pray for their spell list every time they rise. It would be more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T05:25:01-07:00","id":1385237,"title":"","content":"I think there's a half-truth in that, in that 5 is the natural human stat limit. Basically, once you drop to 8th or weaker, you maintain your natural human limit of 5 no matter how much lower you go. That seemed implicit in older editions, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}